hats off to anyone who has to deal with  acrylic nails i couldn't do anything  from cgi muscles to way too tight pants  and even a mouthful of black goop some  thor loving thunder prosthetics and  costumes were harder to bring to life  than they look so whose costume was the  most painful and whose actually wasn't  there at all  number one gore the godbutcher's nails  presented a handful of problems for the  actor christian bale a lot went into  making gore look like a super scary  villain fit for a fan favorite superhero  and some of course creepiest details are  the ones that made bale's life on set  the most difficult according to bale his  attire made him completely incapable of  everything and he cited gore's long  nails as the most difficult part of the  costume to deal with bale called himself  pathetic when trying to sport the  unusually long fingernails in his words  i don't think i can walk because i've  got long nails it affected my brain i  was like i can't eat i've got long nails  despite how difficult dealing with this  costume was it gave bale a newfound  understanding of folks who opt for  particularly decorative hands like gore  i couldn't eat i have a lot of respect  for anyone wearing long acrylic nails  now i couldn't do a damn thing with it  sounds like bale will be keeping the  nail clippers handy from now on  number two the nails weren't the only  part of gore's costume that caused bale  trouble he also had to spend a whole lot  of time in the makeup chair when you see  gore the god butcher it's hard to even  remember that christian bale is in there  somewhere bale is known for being able  to physically transform into different  characters but  gore certainly gave him a run for his  money to transform into the hair-raising  villain bale had to sit in the makeup  chair for three and a half hours every  day and according to him that was after  they shaped the routine down to be more  time efficient he said we got it down to  three and a half hours each morning  myself and three absolutely brilliant  makeup artists creating gore each and  every day between gore scars and spooky  white skin it's no wonder this took ages  number 3 the god of thunder himself got  dangerously close to ripping off his  super tight superhero pants how the  mighty have fallen in a less scary and  more hilarious wardrobe problem thor's  pants were so tight there was almost a  wardrobe malfunction of godlike  proportions thor love and thunder  costume designer mayas rubio paid  special attention to making sure that  thor had a more 80s rock look than his  normal superhero threads that's why she  costumed thor in a t-shirt that left  little to the imagination and pants so  tight that in rubio's words my  assistants were kind of worried there's  nothing that says rockstar quite like  the pants that are so tight it's  worrisome  number four jane's suit has some  aerodynamic details that the other suits  don't most of us watching superheroes on  screen have probably never thought about  how difficult it is for mere mortals to  sport their suits actors actually have  to go through training to learn how to  carry the suit since natalie portman  didn't have that training under her belt  rubio kept her suit on the lighter side  she made sure to use lighter fabrics  with more movement for jane's suit  compared to thor's and she also needed a  much shorter cape that didn't drag  behind 5'3 portman  number 5 if you thought christian bale  had been through enough with this gore  costume already think again it wasn't  easy getting those creepy black teeth in  fact it was downright gross in order to  make gore's mouth look black any pink of  the actual inside of bale's mouth needed  to be covered bale sported a pair of  fake teeth and they were covered with a  sticky substance that made his whole  mouth and tongue look black  number six you may have wondered about  how thor love and thunder brought thor's  hair back to its roots no pun intended  many fans were excited to see thor's  hair back in its og's state of long  flowing locks and if you're wondering if  chris hemsworth is actually blessed with  that head of hair or if it's a bit of  movie magic it looks like that mane is  all him while hemsworth allegedly donned  a wig for the first thor movie about a  year before thor love and thunder  premiered hemsworth posted an adorable  instagram showing him sparring with his  young son while already wearing thor's  long locks and a bun  number seven did you know that jane  foster's helmet wasn't actually there  natalie portman did have a helmet made  especially for her but this helmet was  only worn for her wardrobe fittings and  for photos when she actually filmed  scenes the helmet would have been a bit  too cumbersome to fight in so instead  the helmet was added in in  post-production even when we're looking  right at it we can't tell that that  helmet is cgi  number eight  speaking of natalie portman's superhero  attire her wardrobe was actually  entirely vegan portman is very adamant  about her beliefs and sticking to her  vegan lifestyle so as far as this star  is concerned wearing garments that  required animal cruelty to make are a  no-go according to costume designer  mayas rubio however this challenge was  no problem rubio says that there are  tons of incredible options for someone  looking for vegan textiles instead of  regular leather she went for leather  that was made from a cactus and  according to her it looks exactly like  the real thing number nine thor love and  thunder's main characters weren't the  only folks to get into seriously  intricate costumes and prosthetics and  sometimes it was the other characters  whose costumes presented the most  challenges rubio recalled one particular  costume in the omnipotent city scene  that required a ton of work according to  her she created a mosaic bodysuit for  the actor and then the makeup artist  recreated the design on his face he also  had a massive headpiece that she  hand-placed feathers on ultimately she  says you could only see him on screen  for two seconds but she was still very  proud of that outcome you've really  gotta have attention to detail like that  to make the mcu come alive  number 10 it's easy to forget that  impossible to notice stunt doubles means  double the costumes and when makeup and  costumes are as difficult to make as  they were for thor love and thunder it  means loads of extra work photos of  tessa thompson and her stunt double tara  mackin in their full valkyrie attire  show just how close these costumes are  they're so close in fact that you would  never notice a difference if you  couldn't see their faces and that's why  you almost certainly didn't notice two  valkyries while watching this movie  number 11 a lot went into turning 5-3  natalie portman into a 6-foot tall  superhero jane foster yes natalie  portman is actually on the shorter side  and her character jane is notoriously  tall so how did poorman go from being  the same height as co-star tessa  thompson two towering over her it turns  out she was always standing on a  platform which allowed her to be face to  face with her much taller co-star  hemsworth the more you know  number 12 many fans wonder how portman  got that buff to play jane foster height  wasn't the only major physical  difference between natalie portman and  her character jane portman's arms were  seriously muscular in this movie and  since behind the scenes images showing  portman's arms covered in  motioncapture.surface reddit exploded  with the rumor that jane foster's arms  were more cgi magic than muscle marvel  president kevin feige however insists  that there was no cgi added to portman's  biceps in fact portman worked five days  a week for 10 months working out and  pounding protein shakes to get majorly  bulked up did any of these costume  secrets surprise you what are you hoping  to see return in the next movie tell us  all your thoughts in 